The five frames show the same single dog over time, not multiple dogs. It remains within roughly 1–2 meters of the camera wearer, moving slightly ahead and beside them while sniffing near snowbanks and bushes. No other people are visible. Parked cars, trees, shrubs, and deep snow border the route; the dog occasionally enters the wearer’s immediate walking path. There is no visible injury, emergency, or evidence that the dog is lost.

The most appropriate action is to keep the dog leashed and continue along the cleared sidewalk. This maintains safe control around obstacles and avoids disturbing or endangering others.

